<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch NCM posts H1 profit 13.8 mln guilders.</title>
<headline>Dutch NCM posts H1 profit 13.8 mln guilders.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch credit insurer NCM NV said on Thursday that its first half 1996 net profit was 13.8 million guilders versus a loss of 5.9 million guilders in the same period of 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Insured shipments (billions)    98    vs  96</p>
<p>Premium</p>
<p>    - direct business		  310    vs 327</p>
<p>    - indirect business		 32    vs  30</p>
<p>    - Total				342    vs 357</p>
<p>Claims</p>
<p>    - direct business		  160    vs 158</p>
<p>    - indirect business		 21    vs  23</p>
<p>    - Total				181    vs 181</p>
<p>    Recoveries direct business	25    vs  20</p>
<p>Note - NCM Holding is the holding company for a number of operating companies forming the NCM Group, among which are Nederlandsche Credietverzekering Maatschappij NV (NCM-NL), NCM Credit Insurance Ltd (NCM-UK) and NCM International (NCM-INT).</p>
<p>NCM International has branches in the United States, Denmark, Sweden, Norway, Belgium and Israel.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000 +31 20 504 5040</p>
